From: local
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: bound the retry on a monitor status buffer that never reports DONE

ath11k_dp_rx_reap_mon_status_ring() checks each monitor status buffer for
the HAL_RX_STATUS_BUFFER_DONE tag. When it is absent the driver assumes the
DMA is merely still in flight: it leaves the ring head pointer unchanged,
sets DP_MON_STATUS_NO_DMA and breaks, so the same entry is re-examined on
the next poll.

That assumption does not always hold. Observed on IPQ5018/QCN6122, the
buffer contained HAL_RX_MSDU_END (0xd2) rather than HAL_RX_STATUS_BUFFER_DONE
(0x140) - a valid descriptor of the wrong type, for which the DONE bit is
never going to appear. The ring then never advances and the driver re-reads
the same entry at NAPI poll rate indefinitely, emitting

  ath11k soc:wifi1@c000000: mon status DONE not set d2, buf_id 106

a few thousand times a second until the driver is reinitialised. There is no
escape path: DP_MON_STATUS_NO_DMA is assigned here and read nowhere in the
driver, and the states that are consumed (MATCH, LEAD) are reachable only
under hw_params.full_monitor_mode, which is false for both ipq5018 hw1.0 and
qcn6122.

Count consecutive failures on the same buf_id and, past a threshold, drop
that buffer and let the ring advance - the same recovery the neighbouring
"invalid buf_id" path already performs. A late DMA still gets the original
retry behaviour; only a permanently wrong descriptor is discarded.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
@@ -168,6 +168,8 @@
 	u16 chan_noise_floor;
 	bool hold_mon_dst_ring;
 	u32 mon_status_buf_state;
+	int mon_status_stuck_buf_id;
+	u32 mon_status_stuck_cnt;
 	dma_addr_t mon_status_paddr;
 
 	struct dp_full_mon_mpdu *mon_mpdu;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 #include "dp_rx.h"
 #include "hal_rx.h"
 #include "dp_tx.h"
+
+#define ATH11K_MON_STATUS_STUCK_MAX	8
 #include "peer.h"
 #include "nss.h"
 
@@ -3847,6 +3849,45 @@
 			tlv = (struct hal_tlv_hdr *)skb->data;
 			if (FIELD_GET(HAL_TLV_HDR_TAG, tlv->tl) !=
 					HAL_RX_STATUS_BUFFER_DONE) {
+				if (pmon->mon_status_stuck_buf_id == (int)buf_id) {
+					pmon->mon_status_stuck_cnt++;
+				} else {
+					pmon->mon_status_stuck_buf_id = buf_id;
+					pmon->mon_status_stuck_cnt = 1;
+				}
+
+				/* The hold-and-retry below assumes the DONE bit
+				 * is merely late. If the buffer holds a
+				 * descriptor of an entirely different type it
+				 * will never be set, and re-reading the same
+				 * entry livelocks the ring at NAPI poll rate.
+				 * Give up on it and let the ring advance.
+				 */
+				if (pmon->mon_status_stuck_cnt >
+				    ATH11K_MON_STATUS_STUCK_MAX) {
+					ath11k_warn(ab,
+						    "mon status buf_id %d stuck at tag %lx for %u polls, dropping\n",
+						    buf_id,
+						    FIELD_GET(HAL_TLV_HDR_TAG,
+							      tlv->tl),
+						    pmon->mon_status_stuck_cnt);
+
+					pmon->mon_status_stuck_buf_id = -1;
+					pmon->mon_status_stuck_cnt = 0;
+
+					spin_lock_bh(&rx_ring->idr_lock);
+					idr_remove(&rx_ring->bufs_idr, buf_id);
+					spin_unlock_bh(&rx_ring->idr_lock);
+
+					dma_unmap_single(ab->dev, rxcb->paddr,
+							 skb->len + skb_tailroom(skb),
+							 DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
+					dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+
+					pmon->mon_status_buf_state = DP_MON_STATUS_REPLINISH;
+					goto move_next;
+				}
+
 				ath11k_warn(ab, "mon status DONE not set %lx, buf_id %d\n",
 					    FIELD_GET(HAL_TLV_HDR_TAG,
 						      tlv->tl), buf_id);
@@ -3860,6 +3901,9 @@
 				pmon->mon_status_buf_state = DP_MON_STATUS_NO_DMA;
 				break;
 			}
+
+			pmon->mon_status_stuck_buf_id = -1;
+			pmon->mon_status_stuck_cnt = 0;
 
 			spin_lock_bh(&rx_ring->idr_lock);
 			idr_remove(&rx_ring->bufs_idr, buf_id);
